#### `docs/MINER.md` (Add CLA Signing section)

```markdown
## Contributor License Agreement (CLA)

Contributions to SN118 are MIT-licensed under the Contributor License Agreement. All miners must execute the CLA using their hotkey before uploading agents or model artifacts.

### 1. View CLA Status
Check if your hotkey has signed the current effective CLA:
```bash
uv run ditto cla status
```

### 2. Sign the CLA
To view the text, verify the cryptographic digest, and execute the signature:
```bash
uv run ditto cla sign
```
When prompted, type `I AGREE` to confirm. The CLI creates a deterministic signature:
```
ditto-cla:v1:<netuid>:<cla_version>:<cla_sha256>:<hotkey>:<nonce>:<issued_at>
```
and registers it with the platform.
```

